course: dictionary
lesson: 12492
title: Formal words about money and names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. You meet them in newspapers, official notices and money news, but rarely in playground chat. Denominate is one of them. It can mean to state an amount in a particular money or unit: «The prices in the shop are denominated in pounds.» The clue is the word pounds, which tells you the prices are written in pounds.
explain: Denominate can also mean to give something a name. «The club denominated the new trophy the Golden Cup.» The club is naming the trophy, so denominated means named it. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Two related words are easy to mix up. A denomination is the value of a coin or note, like a £5 note. A denominator is the bottom number of a fraction: in 3/4 the denominator is 4.
fact: Denominate is a formal verb. Its forms are denominate, denominates, denominated and denominating.
fact: «Denominate» means to state an amount in a particular currency or unit, or to give something a name.
fact: «Denominated» means stated in a particular currency or unit, as in «prices are denominated in dollars».
fact: A denomination is the value of a coin or note, like a £5 note.
fact: A denominator is the bottom number of a fraction.
exercise: «The prices in the shop are denominated in pounds.» What does denominated mean here? | Hidden behind the counter | Lowered by half | *Stated in a particular money, like pounds | Stolen from the shop
exercise: Which word means the bottom number of a fraction? | denominate | denomination | *denominator | fraction
exercise: «The club denominated the new trophy the Golden Cup.» What does denominated mean here? | Hid it under the table | Sold it for money | *Gave it a name | Broke it into pieces
test: Which word means the value of a coin or note, like a £5 note? | fraction | *denomination | denominator | denominate
test: Ravi reads «Prices are denominated in euros.» What is the clue to the meaning? | The word prices is the only clue | *The word euros, which is a money unit | Nothing, it is just a number | The full stop at the end
exam: Which sentence uses denominate correctly? | The cat denominated the dog. | *The prices are denominated in euros. | She denominated the rain. | The bus denominates on Tuesdays.
